FIXED. The brief's gate is MET: two full models built, used and closed in one process with
the second creating its global circular buffer, three fresh processes, on BOTH models, at
the full 80-layer shape, all at commit 299440bb276.

--- c-defects attempt 6, 2026-08-31 (supersedes the attempt-3 revision below the line) ---

THE BRIEF'S GATE: "two full models can be built, used and closed in one process, with the
second creating its global circular buffer; three fresh processes."

WHAT IT TOOK, in the order the defects were found and fixed:

  D-C7 as named (L1)    923 776 of 1 393 472 B per L1 bank still allocated after close().
                        Fixed attempt 1 (d40b2093783): a Prefetcher2DContext is captured BY
                        VALUE at module construction, so clearing the owner's _contexts map
                        left every built module holding a context whose global_cb was the
                        live buffer. cleanup() now nulls the field on every context it
                        handed out. Qualified to within 192 B, 3 fresh processes
                        (logs/d11_q_two_pools_run{1,2,3}.log).
  D-C13                 the second model's global CB then failed to allocate: 1 261 952 B
                        free, largest contiguous block 759 488 B, 32 576 B short.
                        Fragmentation. Superseded by 32e552bb0b2.
  D-C14                 the second model's first decode then HUNG: the ttnn program cache
                        belongs to the mesh device, outlives close(), and two structurally
                        identical Galaxy models share compiled decode programs carrying the
                        first model's global-CB addresses. Fixed attempt 4 (faec6e59938):
                        Prefetcher2DConfig.on_global_cb_released ->
                        release_galaxy_global_cb_placement, which retires the mesh's cached
                        programs (and with them 77 stray 32-byte semaphores) and forgets the
                        placement record. See D-C14.status.
  D-C15                 with all of that fixed, QWEN PASSED the gate 3/3 at the full shape
                        (logs/t1,t2,t3, 411/313/321 s) and LLAMA FAILED 3/3 - on DRAM, not
                        L1: 398 617 984 B per DRAM bank of layer weights that close() never
                        released. Fixed attempt 6 (299440bb276). See D-C15.status.

WHERE IT STANDS, measured:

  Qwen, full 80 layers, 3 fresh processes, commit faec6e59938:
      t1_qwen_two_pools_r1   1 passed   411 s
      t2_qwen_two_pools_r2   1 passed   313 s
      t3_qwen_two_pools_r3   1 passed   321 s
  Llama, full 80 layers, both arms, one process, commit 299440bb276:
      z5_probe_full_afterfix 1 passed   626 s   - both models built, used and closed;
      DRAM residue 0 after each; 0 of 240 registered weights retained either time; zero
      "Out of Memory" lines. Before the fix the same shape died 3/3 at layer53_wqkv_ring.

  THE COMMITTED GATE TEST, three fresh processes, both models, commit 299440bb276. It does
  more than build two models: it asserts the two pools' prefill AND decode logits agree at
  PCC >= 0.99 across all 32 slots, so the second model computes the same answers as the
  first through a different block allocation.

      z6_llama_two_pools_r1    1 passed   797.78 s
      z8_llama_two_pools_r2    1 passed  1150.68 s
      z9_llama_two_pools_r3    1 passed   820.22 s
      z7_qwen_two_pools_r1     1 passed   445.81 s
      z10_qwen_two_pools_r2    1 passed   437.29 s
      z11_qwen_two_pools_r3    1 passed   272.24 s

  Six runs, six passes. The same Llama node one commit earlier was rc=124 three times
  (t4/t5/t6), each on a byte-identical DRAM Out of Memory at layer53_wqkv_ring followed by
  an un-drainable teardown that burned its 3600 s bound.

Prefetcher2D's cleanup contract in models/common/modules/README.md is updated for what is
now guaranteed.

--- attempt 3's revision, kept for the record ---
(The "NEXT STEP, on a healthy mesh" it names has been taken; its D-C14 entry is superseded
